  inspectionTitle: "Pamantasan ng Cabuyao \u2014 Student Clearance Handbook & Diary"
  inspectionText: "========================================\nPAMANTASAN NG CABUYAO
    (PNC)\nOFFICIAL STUDENT CLEARANCE HANDBOOK & DIARY\n========================================\nProperty
    of: Senior Year Student (ID #2021-08492)\n\n[PAGE 1: CLEARANCE SIGNING PROTOCOL]\nTo
    officially exit the campus grounds, you must gather all 6 department endorsements
    IN EXACT SEQUENCE:\n  1. Head Librarian (3rd Floor Library Room 308)\n     -
    Resolve overdue borrow records with printed clearance voucher from Room 308 workstation.\n 
    2. Guidance Counselor (2nd Floor Guidance Room 207)\n     - Must demonstrate
    institutional alignment by unscrambling the Core Values sheet.\n  3. CCS Dean
    / Dept Head (2nd Floor Faculty Room 205)\n     - Requires ComLab Hardware Accountability
    Form from 1st Floor ComLab (Room 105).\n  4. University Registrar (Ground Floor
    Window 2 Room 104)\n     - Requires sorting disorganized student grade records
    into archival trays.\n  5. University Cashier (Ground Floor Window 2 Room 102)\n    
    - Requires calculating assessment balance sheet total.\n  6. Executive Vice President
    (Ground Floor Executive Suite Room 101)\n     - Requires retrieving the Official
    University Seal Stamp from 2nd Floor Records Locker.\n  * Final Step: Submit
    completed clearance slip back to Registrar Window 2 to unlock the campus main
    gate!\n\n[PAGE 2: CAMPUS NIGHT PROTOCOL & BLACKOUT ADVISORY]\n- When the sirens
    wail and power drops, ALL classroom doors automatically lock down.\n- Do NOT
    run aimlessly in open hallways. Find a Hallway Locker immediately!\n- Certain
    lockers are secured with padlocks; spare Locker Keys are scattered across faculty
    and librarian desks.\n- While hiding, peer through the ventilation slats and
    remain still.\n- Ground items shimmer periodically and give off a subtle halo,
    even in low visibility.\n========================================"
